You have a very sharp eye! Yes, because we cleaned up and deleted the legacy processAdvancedApproval method in the Service file in the previous step, this Controller will now throw a **compilation error** ("cannot find symbol").
If you look near the bottom of your Controller, you actually have **two** endpoints doing the exact same thing:
 1. @PostMapping("/workflow/approve-reject") (The old one, pointing to the deleted service method).
 2. @PostMapping("/workflow/action") (The new one, pointing to the correct dynamic service method).
### The Fix
You just need to **delete the old, broken endpoint** completely.
Find this block of code (around line 273) and **delete it**:
```java
    @PostMapping("/workflow/approve-reject")
    public ResponseEntity<Map<String, String>> processWorkflowApproval(
            @RequestHeader("Authorization") String token,
            @Valid @RequestBody ProcessVoucherRequestDto dto) {

        String userId = jwtUtil.getUserIdFromToken(token);
        Integer userRole = jwtUtil.getUserRoleFromToken(token);

        log.info("WORKFLOW_ACTION | Batch: {} | User: {} | Action: {}", dto.getBatchId(), userId, dto.getStatus());

        // THIS LINE CAUSES THE ERROR BECAUSE WE DELETED IT:
        voucherRequestService.processAdvancedApproval(dto, userId, userRole);

        return ResponseEntity.ok(Map.of(
                "status", "SUCCESS",
                "message", "Workflow action processed successfully."
        ));
    }

```
### What if my frontend is still calling /workflow/approve-reject?
If you delete that block and your frontend starts getting a **404 Not Found** when you click "Accept" or "Reject", it means your React code is still calling the old URL.
If that happens, simply change the URL string in your frontend API call from "/JS/voucher/workflow/approve-reject" to "/JS/voucher/workflow/action".
Everything else in this Controller is perfectly mapped to the new dynamic engine!
